B1b (2026-11-11), new code; what it re-expresses (no code copied) and the facts it uses:
  UniXNU-piano package/NativeUfs/NativeUfs.cpp (sha256 e7158292b263f8e81fc9e6861d9772f3a76a958acd1f449265d3a025ba986700), whose
    dpuEnable / native_ufs_dpu_map / dpuTlbFlush came from ShengUfs (BSD-2-Clause-Patent): the in-place enable of the display bank
    (translation off -> a table of 1 GiB identity blocks for 2-4 GiB plus 32 MiB windows at 0x10000000, TCR T0SZ 32 with EPD1,
    TCR2 SEP 7 (SEP 0 faulted every IOVA with bit 31 set: sheng i564), MAIR0 attribute 0 = 0x44, SCTLR M|CFRE|CFIE so a fault
    terminates, TLBIALL + TLBSYNC + TLBSTATUS on the bank page, a 50 ms FSR watch of the display's own fetches and the undo), measured
    on SM8550 under the same hypervisor family. DpuSmmu.h is written anew: the stage decided from the bank, IDR2's output size, the
    found SCTLR bits kept, a guard page per window, read-only windows, no self-referencing table, the bank-on take-over through the
    walk, and every step host-tested.
  GopFramebuffer NativeLegacyDisplay.cpp (sha256 e30354b7255fda259a25f3f7f22ecaff8c1c584196f8e54e6c402c03022d5770, listed above):
    the address-only flip (SRC0 + YSTRIDE0 of the scanning pipes, CTL_FLUSH with their bits, no START in video mode), the latch seen
    as CTL_FLUSH reading back 0 (5.4 ms on sheng), the fence before the flip, the LRU windows never evicting the shown or pending
    one, the flip back to the boot memory when the copy runs. DpuFlip.h is written anew for DPU 12's survey path (per-rect offsets,
    multirect, the alpha bit), a vsync interrupt instead of a timer poll, the reverts.
  UniXNU-piano package/PianoDwc3/SmmuStream.h (sha256 8f566938f259730d15407aa2d84abb3f6ec3b06c7bf3dabaef78c7e7fbb930a3): the apps
    SMMU's register offsets and the rule that a store comes from a general register (never wzr) with non-zero values for the TLB
    operations (Qualcomm's trapped SMMU MMIO).
  UniXNU-piano package/common/PianoIrq.h (sha256 ef924cd402caa63f5fe2a46dc2686c2672790f8187a830f13011ab2e6b085a60): used as is
    (SpiLine, Waiter, MissGuard, armcpu_spi_attach): the MDSS SPI 83 and the watch's wake-up.
  ARM IHI 0062 (ARM System Memory Management Unit Architecture Specification, SMMU v2) and the ARM ARM's VMSAv8-64 translation
    table format: the global and context bank registers and fields, the stage 1 and stage 2 descriptors. Public specifications.
  The Linux msm DPU driver (GPL-2.0, specification only, listed above): TOP0 INTR_EN/STATUS/CLEAR at +0x10/0x14/0x18 and that the
  status latches whatever the enable (dpu_hw_interrupts.c), the per-rect source address and stride registers of a multirect pipe
  (dpu_hw_sspp.c), SRCC3_EN. Nothing copied.
